        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pete Ward, Frank Farrell, Bill Devery\n- Organizations: New York Yankees, Baltimore Orioles, Chicago White Sox, New York Highlanders, Major League Baseball\n- Places: Montreal, Quebec, New York City, Bronx\n- Topics: Professional baseball franchise history\n\nFacts:\n- Peter Thomas Ward was born on July 26, 1937, in Montreal, Quebec.\n- Frank Farrell and Bill Devery purchased a baseball franchise that had ceased operations, moved it to New York City, and renamed the club the New York Highlanders.\n- The New York Highlanders were officially renamed the New York Yankees in 1913.\n- The New York Yankees are an American professional baseball team based in the Bronx borough of New York City.\n- Pete Ward is a retired professional baseball player who played nine seasons in Major League Baseball for the Baltimore Orioles, Chicago White Sox, and New York Yankees.",
